    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.04), both of whom benefit immensely from a favorable matchup against Bubba Chandler. **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s score is bolstered by a massive 14% platoon advantage, while **Kyle Tucker** leverages an elite SP Skill rating (+19%) to remain a high-floor producer despite being projected in the lower third of the order. **Andy Pages** (72.93) also enters the conversation as a top-tier play; facing a high-xERA arm in Chandler with a slow delivery, **Andy Pages** is positioned well to leverage his speed, providing the secondary stolen base threat necessary to maintain our category edge.\n\nStrategic optimization was tested at the utility spot, where **Miguel Vargas** (49.51) narrowly secured a start over **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (44.62). While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** offers solid peripheral utility, the optimizer favored **Miguel Vargas** due to his xwOBA profile and a slightly more advantageous lineup position. We are closely monitoring the 37% rain risk in the Mets/Yankees and related matchups, which casts a shadow over **Sam Antonacci**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Miguel Vargas**. Should these games be delayed or postponed, we are prepared to pivot to the bench, though we lack high-scoring alternatives today with **Dominic Smith** and **Wade Meckler** both falling below the 40.0 efficiency floor. \n\nFinally, managers should note that while **Jacob Wilson** (57.99) and **Coby Mayo** (56.02) provide stable, middle-of-the-road production, we are taking a conservative approach with **Liam Hicks**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, as their projected platoon splits against left-handed starters have suppressed their efficiency scores today. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** currently sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the high-upside speed profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Heliot Ramos** to keep the stolen base category competitive while managing our daily efficiency targets.",
